The longer this thread goes on, the longer I realize that it's out of
touch with real games.

In a vacuum, I'd personally prefer "oESP + SDSM + CoMR or "oReflection
+ GDSM + Robe over any "oLS option.  But the more I think about it,
the more I think that's mainly due to hubris; every once in a while I
make a really massively huge mistake, and "oLS would be the high
percentage play _in a vacuum_.

In real life, I get a single early wish pretty often (by early, I mean
pre-Soko).  Going for GDSM gets me a high chance (50% of amulet, 50%
of shield, for 75% chance total) of reflection +MR, and even without
gives me the much more valuable (IMO) MR early on.

In real life, the choice is much more often whether I should blow a
couple wishes re-optimizing for SDSM+Cloak or whatever, or use those
extra wishes getting another marker, conflict, and a host of other
things that are far more valuable than "oLS.

Or to re-phrase:
If I got to the castle with neither MR nor reflection, I'd probably go
for a combo that freed the amulet slot rather than the robe slot.  But
in real life, most well-played characters will wind up with the
opposite because the major pressures are early, and GDSM is such a
massively better choice with a single early wish.


